changelog-videos engine
=======================

Third-party software and assets used by this engine. The setup and `prs doctor` install the packages from npm or
PyPI, and download the models, on first use; none of them is stored in this repository except where noted.

Bundled into rendered videos
- Inter (typeface where Aptos and Segoe UI are missing), SIL Open Font License 1.1, via @fontsource/inter.
- JetBrains Mono (code typeface), SIL Open Font License 1.1, via @fontsource/jetbrains-mono.
- Fluent UI System Icons, MIT License, Microsoft Corporation: the icons the scenes draw are copied into
  theme/icons.js.

Used to make a video
- esbuild (MIT), Playwright (Apache-2.0) with Chrome for Testing, FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL, via imageio-ffmpeg, BSD-2-Clause
  wrapper).
- faster-whisper (MIT) and the Whisper small.en model (MIT, OpenAI) for word timing.
- Kokoro-82M (Apache-2.0, hexgrad) via kokoro-onnx (MIT), the offline narration voice.
- MAI-Voice-2 through Azure AI Speech, when you configure your own Azure resource.
- VS Code Insiders builds, downloaded from update.code.visualstudio.com by `prs digest new` into the cache, and VS Code
  built from microsoft/vscode (MIT) in a release week, to record each change in the real app.

Not distributed
- Aptos is read in place from a local Microsoft Office installation when present; it is never copied into this
  repository or its outputs. Without Office, videos use Segoe UI or Inter.

Microsoft, the Microsoft logo, Visual Studio Code and VS Code are trademarks of Microsoft Corporation. The videos show
the Microsoft logo; use them within the scope your organization allows.

The skill's example (skills/generate-changelog-video/example/) is the changelog video of Oct 19, 2026: its files, and
two review sheets with frames recorded in VS Code Insiders, with the account picture hidden.
